    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` property to the `OwnerDto` schema (right after `locality`), so the code-generated DTO exposes the field with an `Australia/Sydney` example and documented mapping.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added:\n   - `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(toTimezone(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n   - A `REGION_TIMEZONE` map (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `toTimezone(Owner)` method that looks up the already-derived `locality`, returning `null` when the region has no known timezone (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\nThis reuses the existing `toLocality(owner)` derivation (postcode\u2192region, falling back to city), so `timezone` stays consistent with `locality`.\n\n**Verification:** The acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney owner, postcode 2000 \u2192 `locality` \"NSW\", `timezone` \"Australia/Sydney\") passes, and the full `./mvnw test` suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
